ullName":"Rep. Scanlon, Mary Gay [D-PA-5]","party":"D","state":"PA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-06-30","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Stopping the Fraudulent Sales of Firearms Act</strong></p><p>This bill makes it unlawful under federal law to import, manufacture, or sell a firearm or ammunition by fraudulent means (e.g., false representations). Further, the bill makes it unlawful to transmit a wire, radio, or television communication in interstate or foreign commerce related to such a fraudulent importation, manufacture, or sale.</p><p>Under the bill, a violator is subject to federal criminal penalties—a fine, a prison term of up to five years, or both.</p>","updateDate":"2026-11-18T15:37:49Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Stopping the Fraudulent Sales of Firearms Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-11-18T15:41:45Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-11-18T15:41:45Z"}
